This extension adds Rise of the Tomb Raider modding support to Vortex Mod Manager.

The extension will automatically download and install the [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/riseofthetombraider/mods/94]ROTTR Mod Manager[/url], which is used to install and enable/disable ".tiger" mods for the game.
[size=3][b][color=#ffff00]ROTTR Mod Manager does not work for the Epic version of the game[/color][/b][/size]

[b]✅ Supported Versions:[/b]
[list]
[*]Steam[/*]
[*]GOG[/*]
[*]Epic[/*]
[*][b][color=#ea9999]❌ Xbox is NOT supported[/color][/b] because the game files are encrypted and kept in a protected folder that Vortex cannot access.[/*]
[*]Other versions may need to select the installation location manually.[/*]
[/list]
[b]🛠️ Mod Installation Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]ROTTR Mod Manager installs to the game folder, recognised by a "rottrmodmanager.exe" file.[/*]
[*]TR Reboot Mod Manager installs to the game folder, recognised by a "trreboottools.modmanager.exe" file.[/*]
[*]Binaries / Root Folder mods with a ".dll", ".exe", ".tiger", ".asi" or ".addon64" file install to the game folder.[/*]
[*]Mod Manager mods with a "tr2mesh", ".tr2pcd", ".drm", ".skl", ".tr10dtp", ".tr10material" or one of 7 other named files install to the "Mods" folder.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📋 Usage Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]You can open several useful files/folders/URLs using the buttons within the folder icon on the Mods toolbar.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📝 Notes for Mod Authors:[/b]
[spoiler]
Packaging rules for Rise of the Tomb Raider mods, so Vortex installs them to the right place.

Vortex decides what a mod is by looking at the files and folders inside the archive. It tries each installer in order and the first one that matches wins, so archive layout is what determines where your mod ends up.

========================================================================

ROTTR Mod Manager:

Recognised when the archive contains a "rottrmodmanager.exe" file.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

TR Reboot Mod Manager:

Recognised when the archive contains a "trreboottools.modmanager.exe" file.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

Binaries / Root Folder:

Recognised when the archive contains a ".dll", ".exe", ".tiger", ".asi" or ".addon64" file.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

Mod Manager Mod:

Recognised when the archive contains a "tr2mesh", ".tr2pcd", ".drm", ".skl", ".tr10dtp", ".tr10material", ".tr10modeldata", ".t10script", ".t10shaderlib", ".tr10sound", ".dds", ".tr10objectref", ".tr10dtp" or ".tr10anim" file.

  Installs to: "Mods"

========================================================================

Rules That Apply To Every Mod Type:

    - Folder and file name matching is case-insensitive.
    - Extra wrapper folders around a recognised folder are generally fine; the installer searches at any depth.
[/spoiler]
